<%# The arm-by-arm counts one bet was read from, on whichever observable `bet.decided_by`
    names. `unit` is what that observable is measured in, so the same table serves a
    length and a lineage count. %>
<div class="table-scroll" tabindex="0" role="region" id="<%= bet.slug %>-<%= bet.decided_by %>-arms"
     aria-label="Arms of the <%= bet.slug %> sweep, against its control arm">
  <table class="data-table">
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Arm</th>
        <th class="numeric">Emerged runs</th>
        <th class="numeric">Measured</th>
        <th class="numeric">Median peak <%= unit %></th>
        <th class="numeric">Above control</th>
        <th class="numeric">Still rising</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <% bet.arms.each do |arm| %>
        <tr>
          <td>
            <span class="mono"><%= arm.label %></span>
            <% if arm.control? %><span class="badge badge-info">control</span><% end %>
          </td>
          <td class="numeric mono"><%= arm.emerged_count %></td>
          <td class="numeric mono"><%= arm.measured_count(bet.decided_by) %></td>
          <td class="numeric mono">
            <% median = arm.median_peak(bet.decided_by) %>
            <%= median ? number_with_precision(median, precision: 1, strip_insignificant_zeros: true) : "—" %>
          </td>
          <td class="numeric mono">
            <% if arm.control? || bet.control_median_peak.nil? %>
              —
            <% else %>
              <%= arm.above_count(bet.decided_by, bet.control_median_peak) %>
            <% end %>
          </td>
          <td class="numeric mono"><%= arm.rising_count(bet.decided_by) %></td>
        </tr>
      <% end %>
    </tbody>
  </table>
</div>
<p class="text-sm text-muted">
  One row per arm of the sweep. "Emerged runs" counts the arm's confirmed crossings, not
  every crossing the detector flagged, and "Measured" the emerged runs whose samples carry
  the reading after their own crossing; the median is of each run's peak, the highest
  post-crossing reading it recorded. "Above control" counts the runs of the arm whose peak
  is strictly above the control arm's median peak — a dash until the control arm has a
  median to count against — and "Still rising" the runs whose last reading is above the
  median of their own post-crossing readings.
</p>
